Z||000000||NASAReeves||05-18-2001||04:41 PM||||I recently replaced all the bulbs in the tail area of the '88 GT.  All 4 "P-O-N-T-I-A-C" Bulbs, and the other ten, too.  I had read that the ash tray had lights (if so, I knew they had been burnt out for 5 years that I know of)...so I replaced them, too, while I was at it.<P>Don't know if this potential problem is connected or not, but here's what she does now:  When the ignition is off, and I apply the brakes, the ash tray lights come on, along with the dash lights, and the chime goes off!?  This isn't normal for my GT...is it with anybody elses?  Maybe it was the ash tray lights.<P>Also, while I'm on the road & apply brakes, I've noticed that the ash tray lights come on, along with the dash illumination (no chime).  Is this supposed to happen, too?  Ideas or probable cause, if this isn't a standard option?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Scott & Traci<BR>'88 GT||||reg||11
Z||000001||PBJ||05-18-2001||09:11 PM||||What has happened is one of your rear shared tail light brake light sockets has failed and lost it's ground and is now back feeding.<BR>Unplug each brake light one at a time until your problem stops and replace bulb socket.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||05-19-2001||12:35 AM||||COOL!<BR>How did you do it!!!<BR>Actually, you lost a ground in a socket...<BR>Remove the lamps and clean them out with a solvent...<BR>After cleaning the sockets, apply silicone grease to them and try the lights again...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
